"""app_layout.py -- how the app's source in src/ is cut from, and joined back into, canvas_v10.html.

The page has four blocks: one stylesheet and three scripts. Each block is made of the files listed
here, joined in this order, byte for byte. A file starts at the line its anchor begins (a line
start, unique in its block); it ends where the next file starts. The first file of a block starts at
the block's first line.

The engine is ONE closure, (function(){ try{ ... }catch(e){...} })(): its files are slices of that
function, sharing its private variables, so they are joined into one script and never loaded on
their own. _begin.js opens the closure and _end.js closes it.

tools/build_app.py joins src/ into canvas_v10.html (and, with --site, into the multi-file app Pages
serves); tools/split_app.py cuts a canvas_v10.html into src/ by this table. A new file is a new row
here, at the line it starts; a new feature usually goes at the end of its folder's last file or in
a new file of its own, placed where its code sits in the order."""

